      "writtenOn": "2012-08-16T23:28:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Our architecture can have more than one persistent group now.\nAnd, if the target device is different, then the different persistent profile might be created.\nConsidering  the p2p group which multiple clients join, the different persistent profile might be used by the initial setup.\nFor example.\n1. A(to be GO) does go negotiate with B, and then C joins A.\n2. A(to be GO) does go negotiate with C, and then B joins A.\n1 and 2 persistent profiles must be different.\nBased on this, I think it\u0027s better to store the multiple persistent group for one target. \nWhat do you think about ??",
      "parentUuid": "AAAIgX///+Q\u003d",
      "revId": "965932e73f4e1b9a3d3132b5a3ce28a46fc792d1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
